.TH MODINFO 1.SH NAMEmodinfo \- show a module's header.SH SYNOPSIS\fBmodinfo\fRmodule ....SH DESCRIPTIONFor each module named -- one already in memory --\fBmodinfo\fRprints every field of its header in plain words: name, revision, size,owner, access permissions, type and language decoded\fR(\fBTrap handler library   68000 Object Code Module\fR),\fRattributes and revision, edition, the offsets of its entry points anddata, and the stack and data sizes it asks for..nf    Module name           = cio    Module size           = 18058    Type/Language          = 0b01H  Trap handler library ...    Edition               = 6.fi.PPIt calls itself\fBmodule\fRin its usage line.  With no name it answers\fBYou must specify modulename(s)\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOident, mdir, dump